updated_at: "2026-11-07T16:12:10.600Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[61]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T04:32:12.566Z",codex-sol,"Plan: persist the verified candidate before requesting protected squash auto-merge, then exit. An hourly caller and daily catch-up inspect intent without installing dependencies; only a trusted merged candidate enters publication. Serialize all caller events, bind candidate/artifact/run/config identities, and refuse ambiguous registry or provenance results. Full live pilot and account-wide admission evidence remain outside this task authorization; PR will use Refs #249. Run targeted tests, lint and typecheck locally; CI owns the full gate."
  "2026-11-06T04:43:41.909Z",codex-sol,"Implementation now has a dependency-free TypeScript probe, versioned candidate receipt in the bot PR, immutable run artifact retained for 90 days, exact source/digest/config checks and a publication-attempt journal. The hourly path skips installs when no intent exists. Sixteen new focused state/adapter tests pass, including late CI, suppressed bot push, hostile identity, crash recovery and authoritative supersession. Migrating legacy workflow-shape tests to the shared implementation and documenting the read-only fleet inventory."
  "2026-11-06T05:00:39.230Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proofs ran in disposable copies only. Twenty paired regressions each failed with its relevant guard/transition reverted: runner-held merge loop, late CI, stale-base refresh, fork/foreign-branch/exact-head/artifact ownership, merged identity, trusted preparation, required protection, ambiguous publication attempt, live daily cap, downloaded bytes, receipt parsing/schema, authoritative supersession and hourly pilot wiring. Restoring the fixed implementation passed all 20 tests (11 decision + 9 adapter). Targeted package set passed 512 tests with zero failures/skips; lint, typecheck, build:test and docstrings passed; duplication is 0% across 125 sources. Focused release-continuation coverage is 100/100/100/100. Full npm/Bun release gates are delegated to PR CI as requested; no publication, merge, other-repository edit or hosted change was performed."
  "2026-11-06T05:05:45.702Z",codex-sol,"Tightened native protection evidence: enumerate every required context and issuing app from the branch policy, bind the rollup to the exact PR head, and refuse missing/truncated policy evidence. The read-only native reader also succeeded against the existing release PR using the installed gh API transport, without newer checks JSON flags. Focused decision/adapter suite now passes 21/21; its added native-policy regression has a paired behavioral revert. Missing classic policy, moved main, expired artifacts and ambiguous registry absence remain explicit refusals; live publishing identity and fleet-wide capacity admission remain rollout work."
  "2026-11-06T05:14:24.339Z",codex-sol,"Final local targeted command passed 513 tests with no failures or skips. The additional self-pilot resolver fixture passed and failed when its untagged-bootstrap behavior was reverted, bringing the behavioral proof set to 22. The 21 continuation regressions pass after restoration; focused decision coverage remains 100/100/100/100. Pinned pm linked tests (continuation, lint, typecheck) all passed. Canonical publish-attestation audit passed with the shared workflow as the single publisher. Ambient tracker health detects an existing globally discovered extension/CLI version skew; the isolated CI identity passed strict health with required merge drivers. The dependency pin is unchanged. Full npm/Bun gates await PR CI."
  "2026-11-06T05:17:08.468Z",codex-sol,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/250 is open at implementation commit b80ea3a5dc33f23196ff6f730045c4109f86bf39. Initial CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/42167374486 and CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/42167373992 are queued. These are pending receipts, not gate approval. This handoff receipt and claim release will be committed before exact-head CI verification. The task leaves both pm items open; no review bot was requested or awaited. Full issue acceptance remains Refs #249 pending the authorized live pilot, shared-capacity admission tests and fleet rollout measurements."
  "2026-11-06T05:32:32.088Z",codex-sol,"CI on PR #250 reached the full gate and exposed remaining legacy caller-shape assertions plus missing adapter coverage under the unchanged 100 percent thresholds. Reclaimed this item to fix those failures, add complete native/CLI boundary fixtures and re-run targeted coverage. The previous local focused 100 percent claim applies only to release-continuation.ts; the workflow adapter still needs complete measured coverage."
  "2026-11-06T05:46:05.199Z",codex-sol,"CI follow-through fixed all four reported regressions: delegate the remaining changelog assertions to the shared workflow, isolate the version-resolver fixture from caller repository context, use the canonical bounded subprocess adapter, and restore complete coverage. Expanded targeted set passed 552 tests with no failures/skips. Changed release-continuation.ts, scripts/release-continuation.ts and release-caller.ts each now measure 100/100/100/100 under targeted c8 runs. There are 34 continuation tests, each with a paired behavioral revert, plus the self-pilot bootstrap revert (35 proofs total). Lint, typecheck, build:test, documentation and zero-duplication checks pass at unchanged thresholds. Full npm/Bun gates require fresh PR CI after this correction."
  "2026-11-06T06:57:07.393Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: read all five unresolved threads and all comments plus the latest review body (including two follow-ups, the already-published command fixture request and the CI approval pagination concern). Merged current main dependency updates before edits. Valid fixes cover post-release recovery, npm-only OIDC guidance, failed journal writes, ownership-before-parsing, workflow path normalization, pin-specific checks permissions and stale inventory wording. Will add behavioral regressions and self-review the same defect classes. Per the latest instruction, thread replies and resolution are reserved for the orchestrator."
  "2026-11-06T07:05:22.940Z",codex-agent,"Implemented all five reviewed defects and the four additional findings. Post-release hooks now have durable attempt/completion comments; interrupted attempts preserve intent and refuse blind replay. GET 404 alone means absence; every failed write refuses. Discovery checks ownership before parsing, documented qualified workflow paths normalize with strict repository/ref checks, new workflow pins require checks-read while the fixed audited legacy SHA list retains compatibility, CI approval discovery paginates, npm-only OIDC guidance is explicit, and the inventory gap description is current. Initial focused run passes 61 tests. Self-review covered every GitHub mutation and candidate parse path. GitHub REST documentation confirms the path@main response form."
  "2026-11-06T07:12:08.951Z",codex-agent,"Permission compatibility audit: read canonical tag refs and their main-ancestor workflow contents. All 13 released reusable workflow pins have no checks grant; 55 older tags predate that workflow and retain existing checker behavior. The explicit frozen legacy SHA list preserves these pins without guessing a release date, and metadata refresh cannot add future pins to it. New canonical pins lacking checks-read are refused by a dedicated regression."
  "2026-11-06T07:15:33.703Z",codex-agent,"Review regressions pass through the pinned pm test runner: 62 tests, zero failures or skips. Eleven paired behavioral reverts ran only in disposable copies; every mutation failed its targeted test, and restoring the fixed implementation passed that same test. Proofs: post-release completion guard; interrupted hook attempt; success-before-journal crash; recovery workflow wiring; npm-only OIDC docs; mutation-404 guard; ownership-before-parsing; qualified workflow path; new-pin checks permission; approval pagination; already-published coordinate invokes no publish command. Full npm suite initially passed 1548 tests with two existing optional real-data skips but exposed one uncovered completion-refusal branch (99.66 percent adapter branches). Added the missing assertion without lowering thresholds; fresh npm and Bun gates are running sequentially."
  "2026-11-06T07:36:55.351Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 local verification complete. npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed: 1550 tests per run, 1548 passed, zero failed, two existing optional real-data skips; unchanged 100/100/100/100 coverage across all 44 required runtime sources. The later inventory consistency regression passed in the refreshed pinned-pm focused run: 63 passed, zero failed/skipped. Its native CLI regression fails when the stale description is restored in a disposable copy, bringing the review-round paired revert proofs to 12 (each reverted failure and restored pass). Lint, typecheck, build:test, committed dist rebuild, changelog check, 0-percent duplication across 125 sources and 346 documented declarations pass. Strict tracker health with required merge drivers passes under isolated global tracker discovery, with one unchanged advisory telemetry queue warning. All five threads and four review-body findings are fixed. Current main is merged; the next push will require fresh exact-head CI. Thread replies/resolutions, live release acceptance and the fleet wave remain with the orchestrator."
  "2026-11-06T08:24:18.653Z",codex-agent,"Round 2: all seven threads and all comments were enumerated; five earlier threads are resolved and two new findings are valid. Latest review body contains those two findings only. Main and remote branch are current. Plan: return a stranded state rather than throwing on moved source identity; only a fresh current-main probe may retire a provably unpublished and unattempted receipt, preserving its exact candidate under a retired marker. Permit provenance-verified tag/Release repair after main advances without a new npm publication. Reuse an old release branch only after revalidating its owned merged retired PR, retaining the existing push lease. Supersession retires and confirms the receipt before close and propagates failures. Add behavioral reverts and keep the single short no-install reconcile job; thread replies/resolutions remain forbidden."
  "2026-11-06T08:43:04.646Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 implementation: a current-main probe retires only an unattempted, unpublished stranded candidate and preserves its complete receipt under a retired marker. Stale deliveries keep the active receipt. Already-attested npm publication may finish exact tag/Release repair after main moves; attempt and verify boundaries still forbid new publication from stranded state. Branch reuse requires a freshly verified merged bot PR with the exact retired head, followed by the existing push lease. Self-review found that unchanged version/changelog metadata also needs a real PR diff, so preparation now commits a validated run/configuration stamp under .github before packing. Supersession verifies, retires and confirms the old receipt before close; every failed mutation propagates. Targeted state/adapter coverage is 100 in all four dimensions at unchanged thresholds; native Git staging proves the stamp creates a fresh diff even without other metadata changes."
  "2026-11-06T09:00:57.012Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 proofs: 20 paired behavioral mutations ran only in disposable copies; each reverted behavior failed exactly one targeted test and restoring it passed that same test. Covered defined stranded state, attested repair, durable retirement, stale delivery, daily admission output, retired-branch ownership and leased request reuse, changing preparation stamp and no-diff staging, superseded retirement and visible failure, write confirmation, fresh identity, publication boundary, verified successor, stamp validation, prepare-job success despite cleanup failure, complete/unique job enumeration, job run/head binding and original-attempt recovery after rerun. The pinned pm focused command passed 71 tests with zero failures/skips. Changed decision/adapter sources measure 100/100/100/100. Lint/typecheck/build:test pass; zero-duplication gate exposed repeated fixture setup, now factored and verified with three targeted native fixtures at unchanged thresholds. Running the full npm and Bun gates sequentially next."
  "2026-11-06T09:26:47.466Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 final local evidence: both npm run release:check and bun run release:check passed (1562 tests each: 1560 passed, zero failed, two existing optional real-data skips), with unchanged 100/100/100/100 coverage across all 44 required runtime sources. Final pinned-pm focused command passed 71 tests with zero failures/skips after moving stamp creation before verification. The native Git transaction now executes stamp, gate and commit in workflow order; moving the stamp after the gate fails, restoring it passes. This adds the twenty-first paired revert proof. All 21 mutations failed exactly one targeted test and passed after restoration in disposable copies. Final lint, typecheck, build:test, committed dist build, 0-percent duplication over 125 sources, publish-attestation, changelog generation/check and 349 documented declarations pass. Read-only native GitHub attempt/jobs endpoints confirmed the required identity fields on completed CI. Both review findings are fixed; no thread reply/resolution, PR merge, tag, release or npm publish occurred. The next push requires fresh exact-head CI. Live publisher acceptance, fleet admission/timing evidence and migration-wave prerequisites remain open."
  "2026-11-06T09:44:29.014Z",codex-agent,"Owning the remaining review loop from head 2b0c8a9 under the new orchestrator rule. Existing implementation, 21 round-two revert proofs and exact-head green CI remain finished evidence. Queue review through the approved pipeline, inspect every unresolved thread plus outside-diff/nitpick content, fix valid findings with behavioral reverts, push and batch replies/resolutions, then vote all bot comments. No direct bot mentions or PR merge. Stop after a clean current-head review with green CI or five rounds; review wait is bounded to 90 minutes per round."
  "2026-11-06T10:14:18.053Z",codex-agent,"Owned review loop round 1 on 2b0c8a9: completed CodeRabbit review posted seven findings at the current head, with no extra outside-diff/nitpick section. All seven are valid after checking source. Fixes cover exact-commit self-bootstrap for unpublished versions, locale-independent configuration hashing, safe retirement of unattempted stale-base merges, cryptographic provenance and workflow identity validation, and three assertions that were inspecting the wrong source or job. The shared queue log repeated triggers without a terminal line and then reported rate limiting; the completed review object and all seven thread bodies provide the actual review evidence. Will push fixes, batch all thread replies/resolutions, vote every bot comment and re-queue through the approved helper."
  "2026-11-06T10:35:14.653Z",codex-agent,"Review-loop round 1: all seven findings verified. Tools now load exact trusted source plus locked runtime dependencies, with tools SHA bound to the original run and legacy receipt support; configuration hashes use locale-independent ordering; changed squash parent/tree/version can retire only untouched unpublished intent on current main. Sigstore verifies signatures, Fulcio identity and transparency before registry reconciliation, including publish readback and legacy recovery. The three workflow tests now read real defaults, job-level trigger binding and publishing-job preflight ordering. Initial targeted run: 102 passed; new crypto/runtime tests: 5 passed. Focused coverage found three remaining adapter branches; adding positive legacy and native refusal fixtures before final gates."
  "2026-11-06T10:42:21.530Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert evidence in disposable copies: 12 paired proofs each failed once with the relevant behavior reverted and passed once after restoration: unpublished source bootstrap, tools commit binding, locale-independent digest, changed squash source retirement, current-merge retirement, Sigstore signature verification, Fulcio identity, actual changelog input defaults, job-level trigger SHA, native verify stale-trigger refusal, publishing-job OIDC condition and ordering. Self-review also separated the authenticated reusable signer (source run referenced workflow) from the signed caller repository/workflow/ref; public signed fixtures verify the crypto boundary and native transport fixtures assert this identity mapping. Focused five-source coverage reached 100/100/100/100. Zero duplication remains unchanged across 130 sources; docstrings cover 358 declarations. Ambient health shows the pre-existing global extension skew; CI identity health will be checked in an isolated home."
  "2026-11-06T11:03:40.795Z",codex-agent,"The queue completed a second review of the unchanged head and added two valid findings: input/config changes strand old intent before retirement, and the GraphQL branchProtectionRule read can require permissions unavailable to GITHUB_TOKEN. Interrupted the local full gate to incorporate these before the first fix push; it had reached release tests with no release-code failure. The supported REST Get a branch endpoint requires only contents read and exposes required contexts/app IDs; an unauthenticated read confirmed the complete two-check pm-ops policy. Plan: move policy reads there, refuse unsupported active rulesets and incomplete evidence, retain exact-head/review checks, and retire config-changed open/merged intent only with live absence of any attempt/tag/Release/registry artifact. Open intent retirement disables auto-merge first."
  "2026-11-06T11:21:13.091Z",codex-agent,"All nine unresolved findings are addressed. The final disposable-copy proof run completed 30 paired behavioral regressions: every reverted production behavior failed one targeted test and every restored behavior passed one. This includes all seven initial findings, config retirement on open/merged intent with live publication absence and auto-merge disable, contents-read policy enumeration, numeric app binding, and preserving earlier attempts when a receipt changes. YAML mutations were parsed before execution to exclude syntax-only proofs. Focused five-source coverage remains 100/100/100/100 with 87 passing tests; zero duplication is 0/36349 lines across 131 sources; 358 declarations are documented. Read-only native policy verification on PR #250 returned both required checks SUCCESS with no Administration query. The seven-file linked run hit its 120-second timeout under host load; retrying at 600 seconds. The interrupted full gate is not a final receipt."
  "2026-11-06T11:35:49.246Z",codex-agent,"Final security self-review also binds authenticated Fulcio source OIDs to caller repository, merged commit and default-branch ref, independently of the signed JSON and reusable signer SAN. Long repository identities use correct DER string encoding; missing or foreign certificate claims are refused. Verifier caching includes the entire source identity. A native empty-probe fixture runs from a source-only checkout without node_modules and confirms no npm invocation. Current proof receipts: 34 paired behavioral reverts, all 1 failed / 1 restored passed; the affected signature proofs were repeated after certificate hardening. Focused coverage: 89 passed, zero failures/skips, all five changed decision/adapter/runtime/provenance sources at 100/100/100/100. The earlier 120-second linked timeout passed on retry with 112 tests; the final two additions are in the 114-test linked run. No dependency or threshold pin was relaxed. Preparing a single fix push after the bounded full gates."
  "2026-11-06T12:17:54.861Z",codex-agent,"The bounded npm full run exercised 1585 tests: 1580 passed, two optional real-data cases skipped, and three failed. Two were real fixture contracts exposed by this change: dependency-contract now copies the shared workflow it evaluates, and the packed runtime inventory includes Sigstore. The third was the unchanged five-second artifact-reader subprocess timeout under host load; it caused the two unchanged-source coverage gaps in assurance.ts/index.ts. After the fixture updates, all three selected tests passed serially with no timeout increase. The full run is not reported as passing. Every changed release source measured 100/100/100/100 in that full run. Fresh PR CI will certify both npm/Bun full gates after the fix push."
  "2026-11-06T13:02:57.100Z",codex-agent,"Review-loop hardening: all nine findings from the two completed reviews of 2b0c8a9 are valid and fixed. The verifier now authenticates Sigstore signatures, reusable-workflow identity and certificate source OIDs; trusted source tools are bound to the original run; config-change retirement preserves every ambiguous publication attempt; required-check policy uses contents-read REST. The verifier has a separate private locked runtime, with Dependabot and an audit gate. This replaces the temporary production-dependency approach: the earlier Sigstore runtime-manifest proof describes an intermediate revision and is superseded by the private-runtime execution proof. Current receipts contain 36 paired behavioral reverts, each one failing when reverted and passing when restored. A separate private-lock audit revert reports seven moderate vulnerabilities without the security override and zero with it. Empty probes still invoke no npm command. The default linked-test harness timed out without assertion failure under host load; a 600-second retry is running at the same test and coverage thresholds."
  "2026-11-06T13:11:53.897Z",codex-agent,"Final pre-push validation after merging the main release bump: tracker-linked targeted command passed 114 tests, zero failures/skips, on the 600-second retry (the initial 120-second harness timeout had no assertion failure). Focused coverage passed 89 tests with all five changed release sources at 100/100/100/100. The packed CLI and dependency-contract regression command passed two tests; the earlier regular-input timeout also passed its serial retry. There are now 37 paired behavioral revert receipts, each one failing when reverted and passing when restored, plus the private dependency audit revert (seven vulnerabilities to zero). Lint, typecheck, build, test compilation, zero-duplication policy, all 360 docstrings, isolated strict tracker health, production/private audits and dry-run packaging passed. The earlier full npm gate reported 1585 tests, 1580 pass, three failures and two existing optional skips; both fixture defects were corrected and the load timeout passed on retry. No final full-local-pass claim is made; PR CI will certify npm and Bun at unchanged thresholds. Both completed bot reviews were on 2b0c8a9; the fix head still requires fresh CI and queued review. The independent missing-gitHead repair compatibility issue is tracked by ops-release-inventory-gaps. No merge, release or publication action was performed."
  "2026-11-06T15:26:36.535Z",codex-agent,"The queued current-head review completed on ee225b8 with nine further findings. All prior nine threads were answered and resolved; ee225b8 CI passed npm and Bun on Node 22/26 (1585 tests each: 1583 pass, zero fail, two existing optional skips; 47 sources at unchanged 100/100/100/100), both Windows jobs and CodeQL. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/42223979312 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/42223979473 . This next fix batch covers private-lock runtime CI, pre-TypeScript Node-floor checks, protected-context workflow approval, retained concurrency queues, rollback/operator-retirement guidance, fail-closed recovery for non-success checks, bounded Cargo package-table parsing, isolated runtime tests and the workflow audit source label. Third completed full review; two rounds remain in the five-round bound."
  "2026-11-06T15:59:08.933Z",codex-agent,"All nine current review findings are implemented. Fourteen additional paired behavioral revert proofs each failed once under the mutation and passed once after restoration, including actual private-runtime CI installation, runtime/caller/preamble floors, protected-run approval eligibility, retained pending queues, rollback recovery, retirement/publication/hook evidence guards, bounded Cargo parsing, audit source identity and a dependency-free default-test sandbox. The caller-floor proof was repeated after adding the required must-allow corpus for audited legacy callers. This loop now has 51 paired behavioral proofs plus the private dependency audit proof. Targeted tests passed 531 through pinned pm, followed by 17 runtime/caller compatibility tests and 90 focused coverage tests at unchanged 100/100/100/100. Read-only live protection evidence resolved both required checks to workflow run 42223979312 without an Administration credential. Lint, typecheck, zero duplication over 133 sources, all 363 documented declarations, production/private audits and safe package dry-run passed. Final caller/UI wiring checks and changelog/health verification are completing. The next fix push will be queued for bot review immediately, independently of CI, as the updated orchestrator rule requires."
  "2026-11-06T16:05:36.432Z",codex-agent,"Final caller/UI wiring and attestation checks passed 29 tests with zero failures/skips after updating the operator input in the self-pilot, template and migration examples. Final focused coverage passed 90 tests at 100/100/100/100 after preserving audited legacy caller versions; all 14 new revert receipts remain passing. Changelog regeneration/check, release section/date, publish-attestation and lifecycle checks passed at unchanged thresholds. No pm CLI or SDK defect was discovered; no tracker item was closed. The claim is released; fresh bot review is queued immediately after the fix push, and CI will certify the full npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-11-06T16:22:41.790Z",codex-agent,"A final self-review found one more instance of incomplete version evidence: a missing merged package/Cargo file response could fall back to the candidate version. The adapter now refuses that missing live proof before any publication or retirement, while open/config-changed paths retain their existing behavior. The new regression fails with only this guard reverted and passes after restoration. All 54 adapter tests passed; 57 adapter/runtime tests measured the complete changed adapter at unchanged 100/100/100/100. Lint, typecheck, test compilation, zero duplication and all 363 declaration docstrings passed. This is the fifteenth paired proof in the current fix batch, 52 across the owned loop plus the separate dependency-audit proof. All nine ee225b8 threads have verified fix replies and are resolved; votes are complete. The shared queue has not started review of 6606c32, so the next review can cover both fix commits. No merge, release or publish was performed."
  "2026-11-06T21:11:24.787Z",codex-agent,"Resumed after the completed review of ded3953. Existing CI is green. Verify five findings: named Node selectors, open or manually closed intent recovery, expired/deleted preparation evidence, explicit missing Sigstore runtime diagnostics, and bounded release-only discovery. Preserve fail-closed publication and append-only journals; keep local gates targeted and finish before the requested cutoff."
  "2026-11-06T21:30:27.805Z",codex-agent,"All five findings from the completed ded3953 review are valid and fixed. Added obsolete named LTS selector refusal with legacy caller compatibility; shared explicit non-publishing retirement for open, manually closed and merged intent even without preparation evidence; null-safe run/jobs/artifact/tools refusals; clear local Sigstore resolution diagnostics; creator-filtered REST discovery with complete pagination and one probe scan. Open unpublished retirement now confirms closure and permits only exact-head retired branch reuse for a fresh verified leased push, including verified source/config changes. Focused coverage passed 121 tests with zero failures/skips and unchanged 100/100/100/100 across six release modules. Twenty-one paired behavioral mutations ran in disposable copies: every mutation failed one focused test and restoring it passed the same test. Cases cover selector names/normalization, ownership and publication journals, missing preparation evidence, closed intent discovery, confirmed closure, safe branch reuse, bounded bot-only pagination, avoiding duplicate discovery, missing runtime diagnostics and issues-read permissions. No full local suite was started; CI certifies the full gates."
  "2026-11-06T21:33:48.471Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted validation: the tracker-linked eight-file command passed 133 tests, zero failures/skips; focused coverage passed 121 tests at unchanged 100/100/100/100 across six release modules. The final stable creation-order regression separately passed after its paired revert. All 22 paired behavioral proofs ran in disposable copies and each produced one failed mutation / one restored pass: named LTS floor; operator pre-preparation cancellation; retirement preserves publication proof; null preparation run diagnostic; null preparation jobs diagnostic; null artifact fail-closed diagnostic; null trusted tools diagnostic; operator bypasses unavailable preparation only for cancellation; closed unmerged discovery for operator; operator closes open intent; operator confirms closure; bot-only REST discovery; discovery exhausts pages; probe avoids duplicate scan; missing runtime diagnostic; reconcile discovery read permission; selector whitespace normalization; publisher discovery read permission; cancelled branch accepts only fresh leased reuse; stranded intent closes before fresh admission; stranded cancelled branch permits fresh lease; stable bot discovery ordering. PM result tracking remains disabled by existing project policy; counts are recorded here without changing that policy. No publication, merge or hosted change was performed."
